# Windows builds

For Windows setup, builds, or execution-block diagnostics, read
`docs/windows-builds.md` and follow its audit/retry workflow.
Build configuration changes are a last resort: preserve the known-good
toolchain, profiles, features, flags, dependency lock and output location.
Use the established release command; document necessity and rebuild/approval
impact before a required configuration change. Never change configuration,
clean caches or broaden build targets merely to work around execution denial.
Seek one durable IT-approved development policy rather than per-build approvals.
For packaging or distribution, also read `docs/distribution.md`.
Keep those documents as the owners of detailed instructions; do not duplicate
machine paths, dependency counts, or security-policy assumptions here.
